# WN10-CC-000327 - PowerShell Transcription Must Be Enabled

## Description
To comply with the Windows 10 STIG requirement WN10-CC-000327, PowerShell transcription must be enabled. This logs all input and output from the PowerShell console, aiding in auditing and forensic investigations.

## Remediation Steps (PowerShell)

1. Open PowerShell as Administrator.

2. Run the following commands:

New-Item -Path "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\PowerShell\Transcription" -Force

Set-ItemProperty -Path "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\PowerShell\Transcription" -Name "EnableTranscripting" -Type DWord -Value 1

Set-ItemProperty -Path "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\PowerShell\Transcription" -Name "IncludeInvocationHeader" -Type DWord -Value 1

Set-ItemProperty -Path "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\PowerShell\Transcription" -Name "OutputDirectory" -Value "C:\Transcripts"

3. (Optional) Force policy update:

gpupdate /force

